mousepad --help returncode=0
Usage:
  org.xfce.mousepad [OPTION…] [FILES...]

Help Options:
  -h, --help                  Show help options
  --help-all                  Show all help options
  --help-gapplication         Show GApplication options
  --help-gtk                  Show GTK+ Options

Application Options:
  -o, --opening-mode=MODE     File opening mode: "tab", "window" or "mixed" (open tabs in a new window)
  -e, --encoding=ENCODING     Encoding to be used to open files (leave empty to open files in the encoding dialog)
  --list-encodings            Display a list of possible encodings to open files
  -l, --line=LINE             Line number the cursor to position to (LINE > 0 from top, LINE < 0 from bottom)
  -c, --column=COLUMN         Column number the cursor to position to (COLUMN >= 0 from start, COLUMN < 0 from end)
  --preferences               Open the preferences dialog
  --disable-server            Do not register with the D-BUS session message bus
  -q, --quit                  Quit a running Mousepad primary instance
  -v, --version               Print version information and exit
  --display=DISPLAY           X display to use



